  "content": {
    "id": "p24-q18-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "18",
    "prompt": "Abby and Ella ran a 100 metres race, and Abby won by 10 metres. They run a second race, with Abby beginning 10 metres behind the starting line. Assuming both run the same speed as in the first race, who will win and why?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Abby wins. Both reach the 90-metre mark together; Abby is faster, so she finishes the last 10 metres first.",
      "worked": "In the first race, Abby covers 100 metres in the time Ella covers 90 metres, so Abby is faster.\n\nIn that same time during the second race, Abby travels from 10 metres behind the start to the 90-metre mark, while Ella travels from the start to the 90-metre mark. They are level there, with 10 metres left to run. Abby is faster, so Abby wins.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 44
  },
